	(text "RR-HEAD-ACQ  -  Detector-head acquisition board"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5 5)
				(thickness 1)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d4f41738-f555-5c76-889d-c707f95eece4")
	)
	(text "Revision A    Date 2026-11-26    Doc No RR-EL-0103\n\nDetector-head acquisition board: eight SiPM front ends in four identical lanes (floor + reference channel:\npreamp, fast/slow shaping, comparators, event latches), programmable 0-62.5 V bias with per-channel trim,\nfour DACs, STM32G474VET6, isolated RS-485, heater switch, input protection and low-noise rails.\nNetlist: design/circuit.py (stage 1) + overrides.py (stage 2: S2-xx, see STAGE2_CHANGE_REQUESTS.md).\nLanes: sheets LANEk_FLOOR / LANEk_REF / LANEk_LOGIC are identical for k = 0..3 (renamed nets only).\n\nLayers: 6    Thickness: 1.60 mm\nRails: +3V3, +3V3A, +3V3_EVT, +5V6, +5V_A, BUS_GND, FRAME, FRAME_H2, FRAME_H3, FRAME_H4, FRAME_H5, FRAME_H6, FRAME_H7, FRAME_H8, GND\nNet class HV: track 0.25 mm, clearance 1.00 mm, via 0.60/0.30 mm  [HV_BUS, HV_RAW, HV_RAWF, HV_SW, HV_MIR, HV_G, HV_BLD, HV_BFBM, HV_FBM, HV_MDM, HV_CAP, [FR]?_HV1, [FR]?_HVF]\nNet class HEATER: track 1.00 mm, clearance 1.00 mm, via 1.00/0.50 mm  [HEAD_HTR_P, HEAD_HTR_N, HTR_PS, HTR_SW]\nNet class POWER: track 0.40 mm, clearance 0.15 mm, via 0.60/0.30 mm  [GND, +5V_A, +3V3, +3V3_EVT, +5V6, +5V6_A, +5V6_E, +3V3A, +3V3_HV, VIN_*, HEAD_PWR_*, BK_SW, TCXO_VDD, EF_RTN, [FR]?_V5, FRAME, FRAME_*]\nNet class LOOP: track 0.50 mm, clearance 0.20 mm, via 0.60/0.30 mm  [HEAD_LOOP_OUT, HEAD_LOOP_RET, LOOP_A, LOOP_B, LOOP_C]\nNet class ISOLATED: track 0.40 mm, clearance 0.25 mm, via 0.60/0.30 mm  [BUS_*, J2_PRES, SYNC_RX_B]\nNet class DIFF: track 0.25 mm, clearance 0.25 mm, via 0.60/0.30 mm  [RS485_DP, RS485_DN, SYNC_P, SYNC_N]\nNet class SENSITIVE: track 0.20 mm, clearance 0.30 mm, via 0.60/0.30 mm  [[FR]?_A, [FR]?_PINA, [FR]?_PIN, [FR]?_PFB, [FR]?_PG, [FR]?_FS, [FR]?_FFB, [FR]?_TRIM, [FR]?_TPI, [FR]?_SI, [FR]?_SS, [FR]?_SFB]\n\nThis schematic is generated from board.py by tools/eda (rrkicad).\nAll nets are connected by name (global labels / power symbols); there are no drawn wires between symbols."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
